---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../../components/Navbar.astro';
import PageShell from '../../components/PageShell.astro';
---

<Layout 
    title="Editorial Policy & Reference Standards | Real BMI"
    description="Read our editorial policy for evidence-based health content, peer-reviewed methodology, clinical screening definitions, and transparent user guidance."
>
    <Navbar />
    <PageShell
      title="Editorial Policy"
      eyebrow="Methodology & Transparency"
      description="How our editorial team researches, references, and maintains evidence-based health tools and educational content."
      returnUrl="/en/"
      returnLabel="Home"
    >
        <p>At <strong>Real BMI</strong>, an independent health calculator platform maintained by the <strong>Real BMI Editorial Team</strong>, the goal is to provide clear, transparent, and reference-based health calculators to help individuals estimate their body mass index, basal metabolic rate, total daily energy expenditure, and complementary body metrics.</p>

        <h2>1. Evidence-Based Reference Guidelines</h2>
        <p>All formulas, reference ranges, and health metrics published across our platform are derived from established mathematical equations and public health guidelines established by recognized global health organizations, including:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>World Health Organization (WHO):</strong> Global Obesity Classifications, South-East Asia Ethnic BMI Cut-offs (23.0 kg/m²), and Waist-to-Hip Ratio guidelines.</li>
          <li><strong>Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC):</strong> Adult BMI Formula Standards and Pediatric Growth Percentile Reference Charts.</li>
          <li><strong>National Institutes of Health (NIH):</strong> Published body surface area and metabolic energy equations.</li>
          <li><strong>Peer-Reviewed Research:</strong> Equations published by researchers (such as Mifflin-St Jeor, Harris-Benedict, Boer, Devine, Mosteller, and Epley).</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>2. Content Creation & Maintenance</h2>
        <p>The website is created and maintained independently by the Real BMI Editorial Team:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Editorial Maintenance:</strong> Real BMI Editorial Team</li>
          <li><strong>Methodology Basis:</strong> Published mathematical formulas and public health reference guidelines</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3. Transparency & Continuous Updates</h2>
        <p>We periodically review published guidelines and update calculators and articles when relevant reference standards change. We update our calculators and health articles to reflect published consensus guidelines. Each reference article specifies its citations and sources.</p>

        <h2>4. Independence & Commercial Integrity</h2>
        <p>This platform operates as an independent calculator project. Content decisions are made without pharmaceutical or commercial sponsorship influence.</p>

        <h2>5. Educational Disclaimer</h2>
        <p>The metrics provided on this site (including BMI, BMR, TDEE, and body fat percentage estimates) serve as educational estimates for planning and personal reference. This platform is not a medical practice, hospital, clinic, or physician-reviewed service, and does not provide formal medical diagnosis or treatment advice. Always consult a licensed healthcare provider for personal health concerns.</p>

        <h2>6. Semi-Annual Review Cycle & Fact-Checking Process</h2>
        <p>We maintain a rigorous semi-annual audit protocol for every published formula, table, and reference range. When global organizations such as the WHO, CDC, or ICMR publish updated statistical benchmarks or clinical guidelines, our computational engines and educational documentation are reviewed and re-verified against official whitepapers. Every formula implementation undergoes automated unit and boundary testing before deployment to ensure numerical precision across both metric and imperial systems.</p>

        <h2>7. Originality, Human Authorship & Anti-Scraping Commitment</h2>
        <p>All written guides, worked examples, step-by-step mathematical walkthroughs, and FAQ responses are authored originally by the Real BMI Editorial Team with careful reference to cited primary sources. We strictly reject content scraping, mass synthetic boilerplate generation, and repetitive keyword stuffing. Every article is designed to provide actionable, authentic educational value tailored specifically to user search intent.</p>

        <h2>8. Corrections, User Inquiries & Errata Policy</h2>
        <p>We are committed to absolute transparency and algorithmic accountability. If you identify a potential mathematical discrepancy, an ambiguous definition, or an outdated citation in any calculator or guide, we encourage direct reporting via our Contact page. Verified corrections are promptly investigated, resolved in source code, and logged in our production version notes.</p>

        <h2>9. Pre-Publication Content Review & User Privacy Protocol</h2>
        <p>To maintain clear explanations and mathematical accuracy, each calculator, guide, and reference chart undergoes a pre-publication review process:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Step 1: Evidence & Citation Check:</strong> All medical formulas, health thresholds, and reference charts are cross-checked against authoritative source literature (WHO, CDC, NHLBI).</li>
          <li><strong>Step 2: Mathematical Precision Audit:</strong> Algorithmic conversions and rounding logic are verified against edge cases (boundary test suites) in both metric and imperial systems.</li>
          <li><strong>Step 3: Privacy & Data Security Screening:</strong> A mandatory privacy audit ensures that no personal identifying details—including names, email addresses, phone numbers, or private user credentials—are ever logged, stored, or exposed in public entries, calculator inputs, or URL parameters.</li>
          <li><strong>Step 4: Final Review:</strong> All content is reviewed for accuracy, formatting, references, and privacy before publication.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </PageShell>
</Layout>
